#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a81c1cd-7381-5788-8a51-53cecee5f600" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Lines Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082e1fb8-38d1-5dd8-8994-bb44202783c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560379} {:answer/id #uuid "239b4a9b-56e4-5a86-8a68-9c399e4eaa37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560447} {:answer/id #uuid "7014a716-ba56-5a31-b1a8-377a659ba2df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-\\frac{3}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560601} {:answer/id #uuid "95309e0e-fd50-5c5e-b095-3c20e548ce32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{3}{2},2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560670} {:answer/id #uuid "ee62bf3c-cdf7-51b8-b6f8-f8df94a25f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee62bf3c-cdf7-51b8-b6f8-f8df94a25f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560830} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d4432d3-c731-55d8-bd24-6b2c198e1059" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1dae329-b51c-5003-8d13-154486e1f8af" :question/math-academy-id "q-60172" :question/problem "Find the point of intersection of the lines $3x+4y=1$ and $2x-2y=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the system of equations consisting of the two lines:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y=1 \\\\ 2x-2y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the second equation by $2,$ then we will get a $-4y$ term that can cancel with the $4y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y=1 &  \\\\ 2x-2y=3 & |\\,\\times 2\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+4y=1 \\\\ 4x-4y=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\cancel{4y} & =1 \\\\ 4x-\\cancel{4y} & =6 \\\\ (3x+4x) & =(1+6) \\\\ 7x & =7 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=1$ into the equation $2x-2y=3$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-2y & =3 \\\\ 2(1)-2y & =3 \\\\ 2-2y & =3 \\\\ -2y & =1 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=1,\\,y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ So the coordinates of the point of intersection are $(1,-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068715 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b154eb5d-a45b-5d92-9e33-dd7875327e6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Unknown Parameters Given a Point of Intersection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011c4ed3-b08e-5bb4-8d64-714af50167c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560361} {:answer/id #uuid "156f3b79-c1f4-564c-9343-71d9780571e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0,\\,b=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560409} {:answer/id #uuid "46ace411-49e7-5267-8ce7-27b0b740cb4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=3,\\,b=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560519} {:answer/id #uuid "602e967c-a929-567a-9257-15cb77561af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-2,\\,b=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560571} {:answer/id #uuid "6a59c9dc-7269-58a8-99a5-540b40f347b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=4,\\,b=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011c4ed3-b08e-5bb4-8d64-714af50167c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=-3,\\,b=-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560361} :answer-field/id #uuid "799a5806-fdb3-56b9-abdb-217c2f17b6fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea2f44ab-dddd-5fb6-b2ba-34d59e15c7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-60182" :question/problem "The lines $y=3x-b$ and $y=x+5$ intersect at the point $C$ with coordinates $(a,2).$ Find the parameters $a$ and $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $(a,2)$ is the point of intersection of the two lines, the values $x=a,\\,y=2$ must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=3x-b \\\\ y=x+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=a,\\,y=2$ to obtain a new system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2=3a-b \\\\ 2=a+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $a$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =a+5 \\\\ -3 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $a=-3$ into the first equation and solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3a-b \\\\ 2 & =3(-3)-b \\\\ 2 & =-9-b \\\\ 11 & =-b \\\\ -11 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3$ and $b=-11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4a81c1cd-7381-5788-8a51-53cecee5f600" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Lines Given in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08848abb-4fdd-54a8-a134-d62409d65dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560381} {:answer/id #uuid "146b7b45-9602-56bf-9589-403ec424c06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560407} {:answer/id #uuid "7f322004-2d74-5c3e-ab36-7b710e50faaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560635} {:answer/id #uuid "93ad6313-5531-5f5e-b1e8-0e7aa0bd953c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560668} {:answer/id #uuid "a20276d7-269b-565c-a947-89053ba18c09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "146b7b45-9602-56bf-9589-403ec424c06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560407} :answer-field/id #uuid "906a9694-dc14-5b8b-9fcf-596a282ca62d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e70442d3-8437-54dd-ba25-74163c48588a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75873" :question/problem "Find the point of intersection of the lines $2x+y=12$ and $x-2y=6.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the system of equations consisting of the two lines:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=12 \\\\ x-2y=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the elimination method to solve the system. Notice that if we multiply the first equation by $2,$ then we will get a $2y$ term that can cancel with the $-2y$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y=12 & |\\,\\times 2 \\\\ x-2y=6 & \\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=24 \\\\ x-2y=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations eliminates the $y$-variable and allows us to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+\\cancel{2y} & =24 \\\\ x-\\cancel{2y} & =6 \\\\ (4x+x) & =(24+6) \\\\ 5x & =30 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can substitute $x=6$ into the equation $x-2y=6$ to solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y & =6 \\\\ 6-2y & =6 \\\\ -2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system is $x=6,\\,y=0.$ So the coordinates of the point of intersection are $(6,0).$"}]}
